===============================

This is the README for GNU awk 5 in the WSL
(Windows Subsystem for Linux) environment of MS-Windows

    What follows has been tested using an Ubuntu WSL distribution,
but should work also for other WSL distributions.

    Gawk has been compiled and tested using the standard Linux
tools.  One does not need to use "sudo" for a personal installation,
but should be able to become super-user to install the build.

	tar -xvpzf gawk-5.4.x.tar.gz
	cd gawk-5.4.x
	./configure && make

    In itself, gawk can be built everywhere, i.e., inside or outside
the Linux file System.  But see below.

Testing and installing gawk
---------------------------

    The command "make check" in the WSL environment can give different
results if the gawk executable is inside the Linux file system, or
outside it.  Since outside the Linux file system the "inodes" are
simulated, and not "the real thing", a few tests can fail (and their
failure is ignored).  Inside the Linux file system (e.g., in a home
directory), all the tests should succeed.

    Running "make install" requires "root" capabilities (of course).
The installed version goes into /usr/local/bin, which takes precedence
with the version of gawk that comes with WSL, and resides in /usr/bin.

    If MPFR support is desired, the required libraries should be present
in the WSL environment.

